1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:07,654
Do you know a show called
<i>Document Memoreal</i>?

2
00:00:07,737 --> 00:00:09,697
It's that famous
day-in-the-life show, right?

3
00:00:09,781 --> 00:00:12,742
That show called and said
they want to do a feature on me.

4
00:00:12,826 --> 00:00:14,661
Say what?

5
00:00:14,744 --> 00:00:17,831
Good morning.
I'm Torihara from <i>Document Memoreal</i>.

6
00:00:17,914 --> 00:00:19,499
Why those outfits and makeup?

7
00:00:19,582 --> 00:00:21,000
We thought we might be on camera too.

8
00:00:21,084 --> 00:00:22,544
I look forward to working with you all!

9
00:00:22,627 --> 00:00:24,796
-The pleasure is ours!
-Thank you.

10
00:00:24,879 --> 00:00:25,713
<i>Wow.</i>

11
00:00:25,797 --> 00:00:27,173
<i>What a handsome man.</i>

12
00:00:27,257 --> 00:00:29,717
<i>To be honest, he is an idiot,</i>

13
00:00:29,801 --> 00:00:33,471
but he works really hard
to get acting jobs.

14
00:00:33,555 --> 00:00:37,475
Everyone is supporting me,
so I want to get on top.

15
00:00:37,559 --> 00:00:40,395
It's good. But if we inflate his ego more,
we can film something way funnier.

16
00:00:40,478 --> 00:00:42,355
<i>It's better to exaggerate things.</i>

17
00:00:42,856 --> 00:00:45,775
<i>I have already sufficiently</i>
<i>captured your charm.</i>

18
00:00:45,859 --> 00:00:47,652
<i>Look forward to the broadcast.</i>

19
00:01:21,311 --> 00:01:24,230
-Midori, it's starting, hurry!
-Wait for me!

20
00:01:24,814 --> 00:01:27,066
Hey, you're looking so restless.

21
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:29,027
-Well, of course I would be.
-Right?

22
00:01:29,110 --> 00:01:30,028
Thank you.

23
00:01:30,528 --> 00:01:32,280
-Thanks.
-Thank you.

24
00:01:36,367 --> 00:01:37,702
-There it is.
-It's started!

25
00:01:37,785 --> 00:01:39,245
So cool, Konta!

26
00:01:41,456 --> 00:01:44,375
THE UNEMPLOYED DREAM-CHASER
NO MATTER WHAT, I STILL WANT TO ACT

27
00:01:44,459 --> 00:01:46,461
<i>What's with this subtitle?</i>

28
00:01:49,214 --> 00:01:50,256
Hello.

29
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:51,591
I'm the actor--

30
00:01:54,010 --> 00:01:57,096
Hello. I'm the actor, Konta… Wait.

31
00:01:58,598 --> 00:01:59,933
I'm the actor…

32
00:02:00,642 --> 00:02:01,768
Konta Hoshino.

33
00:02:01,851 --> 00:02:03,645
<i>Do you know this person?</i>

34
00:02:03,728 --> 00:02:04,604
We're rolling!

35
00:02:04,687 --> 00:02:06,856
<i>Hoshino Konta, 33 years old.</i>

36
00:02:09,025 --> 00:02:11,945
-Run away!
-So you have come, Poseidon.

37
00:02:12,654 --> 00:02:13,780
Everyone, it's okay.

38
00:02:14,489 --> 00:02:17,408
I will protect this hospital.

39
00:02:17,492 --> 00:02:18,451
Cut!

40
00:02:19,202 --> 00:02:21,079
-Hey, run away!
-Yes?

41
00:02:21,162 --> 00:02:24,082
-You're an extra, just run away!
-Oh, sorry.

42
00:02:24,165 --> 00:02:27,418
-But I acted with my soul…
-No, just do what you're told to do.

43
00:02:27,502 --> 00:02:29,128
-I'm sorry.
-Don't do anything extra!

44
00:02:29,212 --> 00:02:30,171
Yes! I'm sorry!

45
00:02:30,255 --> 00:02:31,464
Okay, one more time!

46
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:35,718
<i>His only roles have been extras</i>
<i>in stage plays and TV shows,</i>

47
00:02:35,802 --> 00:02:38,263
<i>and his talents haven't blossomed.</i>

48
00:02:38,346 --> 00:02:41,224
<i>A self-proclaimed actor.</i>

49
00:02:41,307 --> 00:02:42,517
Self-proclaimed?

50
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:44,435
They're so mean from the get-go!

51
00:02:47,563 --> 00:02:49,691
This is a really magnificent villa.

52
00:02:49,774 --> 00:02:53,486
Well, it's really nothing!

53
00:02:54,237 --> 00:02:55,905
Not a big deal, okay?

54
00:02:56,656 --> 00:03:01,160
<i>Konta lives in this villa,</i>
<i>which was owned by his late grandmother.</i>

55
00:03:02,078 --> 00:03:04,372
<i>Since he can stay rent-free,</i>

56
00:03:04,455 --> 00:03:07,750
<i>it is a huge help for Konta,</i>
<i>who hasn't made it big yet.</i>

57
00:03:10,545 --> 00:03:13,089
Has the narrator been decided yet?

58
00:03:13,172 --> 00:03:14,674
Oh, not yet.

59
00:03:14,757 --> 00:03:17,719
Then please get Koji Yakusho.

60
00:03:17,802 --> 00:03:20,263
No, I don't think we can…

61
00:03:20,346 --> 00:03:22,098
Just ask him, just in case.

62
00:03:22,181 --> 00:03:25,935
Narration is very important for
a documentary. Get someone good!

63
00:03:26,561 --> 00:03:30,732
<i>Konta, we are sorry</i>
<i>we couldn't meet your request.</i>

64
00:03:30,815 --> 00:03:33,151
<i>All you've got is me, Wakana Matsumoto.</i>

65
00:03:33,234 --> 00:03:34,569
<i>Please forgive us.</i>

66
00:03:35,194 --> 00:03:39,157
Hey, if they edit it like that,
it will make me look bad.

67
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,241
Who goes there?

68
00:03:48,291 --> 00:03:54,589
<i>Konta uses this entire villa</i>
<i>as a space for his personal training.</i>

69
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:08,978
You bastard! Come on!

70
00:04:09,062 --> 00:04:13,649
<i>He seriously practices</i>
<i>using past masterpieces as a model.</i>

71
00:04:15,526 --> 00:04:16,903
Isn't this too mean?

72
00:04:16,986 --> 00:04:18,404
This is bad.

73
00:04:18,488 --> 00:04:21,532
The editing is just malicious, isn't it?

74
00:04:25,244 --> 00:04:28,456
<i>Konta got tired from playing make-believe.</i>

75
00:04:29,082 --> 00:04:31,751
<i>He fell asleep while doing Zen meditation.</i>

76
00:04:31,834 --> 00:04:33,086
Playing make-believe?

77
00:04:33,169 --> 00:04:35,630
I wasn't sleeping.
That was mental concentration!

78
00:04:36,214 --> 00:04:38,257
I'm being made a fool of!

79
00:04:38,341 --> 00:04:40,635
The sea feels good, right?

80
00:04:40,718 --> 00:04:42,845
-It's nice.
-Pleasant, right?

81
00:04:44,472 --> 00:04:45,640
Wait a second…

82
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:51,604
For us actors,
our bodies are our greatest asset.

83
00:04:51,687 --> 00:04:55,983
So… I spare nothing…
when it comes to training.

84
00:04:56,067 --> 00:04:59,070
Twenty, forty, fifty… Okay.

85
00:05:01,447 --> 00:05:05,493
<i>He chooses vegetables that he can buy</i>
<i>with the little money he has.</i>

86
00:05:05,576 --> 00:05:06,911
Cut that part.

87
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:12,166
So good.

88
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:15,128
How poor do they want to make me look?

89
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:19,757
I can really taste the sun.

90
00:05:19,841 --> 00:05:22,385
<i>Then, a savior appeared!</i>

91
00:05:22,468 --> 00:05:28,307
Mr. Konta. I was just about
to come over and deliver some fish.

92
00:05:28,391 --> 00:05:32,728
<i>The one who saves</i>
<i>penniless actor Konta from poverty</i>

93
00:05:33,479 --> 00:05:37,900
<i>is the one who manages the villa grounds,</i>
<i>the caretaker Mr. Nishigami.</i>

94
00:05:37,984 --> 00:05:39,819
But, I'm doing an interview.

95
00:05:39,902 --> 00:05:41,737
<i>I want him to manage me too.</i>

96
00:05:41,821 --> 00:05:44,157
-Hey, are you filming me?
-Yes.

97
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:47,743
Hey, what was that just now?
Did she let her true desires out a bit?

98
00:05:57,086 --> 00:05:58,462
The heck?

99
00:05:59,213 --> 00:06:01,966
Mr. Torihara betrayed me.

100
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,678
He didn't look like
such a bad person, though.

101
00:06:05,761 --> 00:06:08,097
No, this editing speaks volumes.

102
00:06:08,181 --> 00:06:09,932
It's like a smear campaign.

103
00:06:12,018 --> 00:06:15,188
<i>Bringing you delicious milk every day!</i>

104
00:06:15,271 --> 00:06:16,981
CONNECTING HEARTS
HIROKAMI DAIRY

105
00:06:18,566 --> 00:06:23,446
<i>The one who saves</i>
<i>penniless actor Konta from poverty</i>

106
00:06:23,529 --> 00:06:28,117
<i>is the one who manages the villa grounds,</i>
<i>the caretaker Mr. Nishigami.</i>

107
00:06:28,201 --> 00:06:31,245
Why are they bridging the ad break
with this video of Mr. Nishigami?

108
00:06:34,123 --> 00:06:38,628
<i>When night falls,</i>
<i>jobless youths gathered at the villa.</i>

109
00:06:38,711 --> 00:06:40,213
Jobless?

110
00:06:40,838 --> 00:06:44,592
This is <i>acqua pazza</i> made with
the sea bream Mr. Nishigami brought us.

111
00:06:45,176 --> 00:06:46,761
These are ordinary people.

112
00:06:46,844 --> 00:06:49,013
<i>Even though</i>
<i>he hasn't made it big as an actor</i>

113
00:06:49,096 --> 00:06:52,725
<i>and has no work, Konta seems happy.</i>

114
00:06:53,434 --> 00:06:56,562
<i>Happiness comes in</i>
<i>different forms for everyone.</i>

115
00:06:58,689 --> 00:07:00,650
<i>Today we're having a barbecue!</i>

116
00:07:00,733 --> 00:07:03,069
<i>Today's meat is top grade</i>

117
00:07:03,152 --> 00:07:06,906
<i>We are unemployed, living on benefits!</i>

118
00:07:06,989 --> 00:07:09,325
Hey, this is terrible! I wanna die!

119
00:07:10,076 --> 00:07:11,494
<i>Benefits!</i>

120
00:07:11,577 --> 00:07:15,164
<i>And so, these youths</i>
<i>who have given up on working</i>

121
00:07:15,248 --> 00:07:18,084
<i>kept on drinking the night away.</i>

122
00:07:18,751 --> 00:07:20,461
How horrible!

123
00:07:21,045 --> 00:07:22,004
Konta!

124
00:07:22,088 --> 00:07:23,881
I have some tea here.
Make sure to drink it.

125
00:07:23,965 --> 00:07:25,174
Oh, thank you.

126
00:07:25,258 --> 00:07:28,052
Heave-ho!

127
00:07:28,135 --> 00:07:30,471
<i>When he doesn't have acting work,</i>

128
00:07:30,555 --> 00:07:34,934
<i>Konta makes a living</i>
<i>by helping out the local elderly.</i>

129
00:07:35,643 --> 00:07:38,479
Oh, what is this? Did he secretly film me?

130
00:07:39,605 --> 00:07:40,690
Wow, it's good.

131
00:07:40,773 --> 00:07:43,818
-I can't stop.
<i>-Was he hungry?</i>

132
00:07:43,901 --> 00:07:46,696
<i>Unable to resist,</i>
<i>Konta ended up eating weeds.</i>

133
00:07:47,488 --> 00:07:48,447
Konta!

134
00:07:48,531 --> 00:07:49,907
No, you got it wrong.

135
00:07:49,991 --> 00:07:52,076
-It's mugwort!
-Huh?

136
00:07:52,159 --> 00:07:54,996
Wait, Pero!

137
00:07:55,079 --> 00:07:56,622
Pero!

138
00:07:56,706 --> 00:07:58,708
Pero, Wait!

139
00:07:58,791 --> 00:08:00,585
Pero!

140
00:08:02,545 --> 00:08:04,171
Okay, let me hold you.

141
00:08:04,255 --> 00:08:07,758
<i>-Konta is being looked down on by a dog.</i>
-Oh, no!

142
00:08:07,842 --> 00:08:08,926
Looked down on?

143
00:08:09,010 --> 00:08:10,553
Literally or metaphorically?

144
00:08:10,636 --> 00:08:12,388
Both, I think.

145
00:08:12,471 --> 00:08:13,306
Heave-ho.

146
00:08:14,307 --> 00:08:15,558
Heave-ho!

147
00:08:20,396 --> 00:08:24,275
<i>Now, he is literally eating dirt.</i>

148
00:08:24,358 --> 00:08:26,569
Well, that was clever.

149
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:28,863
That's right.

150
00:08:28,946 --> 00:08:32,533
By the way, Mr. Jin,
give me some work once in a while.

151
00:08:32,617 --> 00:08:35,161
No matter how small the role…
Even a tiny role. I'll do it.

152
00:08:35,244 --> 00:08:39,040
<i>Konta is close friends</i>
<i>with the popular actor Jin Ichijo.</i>

153
00:08:39,749 --> 00:08:41,709
<i>To this older colleague,</i>

154
00:08:41,792 --> 00:08:45,755
<i>he throws away his pride</i>
<i>and desperately begs</i>

155
00:08:46,339 --> 00:08:51,177
<i>for a job, even a tiny part.</i>

156
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:53,137
I told them to cut this part!

157
00:08:56,515 --> 00:08:58,934
WHY DID YOU DECIDE TO BECOME AN ACTOR?

158
00:08:59,018 --> 00:09:04,523
When I was in the third grade,
I acted in <i>Momotaro </i>for a school play.

159
00:09:04,607 --> 00:09:06,192
-Out of focus.
<i>-At that time…</i>

160
00:09:06,275 --> 00:09:07,777
It's out of focus.

161
00:09:07,860 --> 00:09:10,404
Can you even see me?

162
00:09:10,488 --> 00:09:11,989
You can't see me, right?

163
00:09:12,073 --> 00:09:13,282
It's just the fire!

164
00:09:13,366 --> 00:09:15,951
It's just the fire the whole time!
The fire!

165
00:09:16,035 --> 00:09:17,620
This is a documentary about fire!

166
00:09:17,703 --> 00:09:20,164
<i>-…to me, was a very happy moment.</i>
<i>-Fire!</i>

167
00:09:20,247 --> 00:09:21,207
<i>A fire documentary!</i>

168
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:23,250
I was born to act.

169
00:09:23,334 --> 00:09:26,337
<i>Out of focus!</i>

170
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:28,381
<i>I truly believe that.</i>

171
00:09:28,464 --> 00:09:30,549
<i>Hey, where even am I in this shot?</i>

172
00:09:31,801 --> 00:09:33,302
<i>Me? What about me?</i>

173
00:09:33,386 --> 00:09:36,806
Midori also supports me.

174
00:09:38,099 --> 00:09:41,060
Everyone is supporting me,
so I want to get on top…

175
00:09:41,852 --> 00:09:44,230
<i>I was saying something good!</i>

176
00:09:53,531 --> 00:09:55,074
Konta!

177
00:09:55,157 --> 00:09:56,492
Get up!

178
00:09:57,076 --> 00:09:59,620
<i>Stop it! Please stop it!</i>

179
00:10:02,123 --> 00:10:03,708
The heck is this?

180
00:10:03,791 --> 00:10:06,419
This editing is way too mean.

181
00:10:10,965 --> 00:10:12,258
Konta?

182
00:10:22,643 --> 00:10:23,561
It's dangerous.

183
00:10:23,644 --> 00:10:29,692
<i>Out of a misguided sense of purpose,</i>
<i>Konta chose the path of an actor.</i>

184
00:10:30,693 --> 00:10:33,696
<i>Although he currently</i>
<i>has no money or work,</i>

185
00:10:33,779 --> 00:10:36,699
<i>with his characteristic</i>
<i>groundless confidence,</i>

186
00:10:36,782 --> 00:10:38,826
<i>he has come far.</i>

187
00:10:40,870 --> 00:10:45,082
<i>However, Konta's groundless confidence</i>

188
00:10:45,166 --> 00:10:48,711
<i>also gives energy</i>
<i>to the people around him.</i>

189
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:52,006
Mr. Torihara. I'll make you a drink.

190
00:10:52,089 --> 00:10:54,216
But I'm still on the clock.

191
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:55,926
It's totally fine.

192
00:10:56,010 --> 00:10:59,180
However, if you drink this,
you'll turn stupid!

193
00:10:59,263 --> 00:11:00,306
What?

194
00:11:00,389 --> 00:11:03,142
Wait, Konta, that's way too much.

195
00:11:03,225 --> 00:11:06,145
Mr. Torihara has been filming me
all day today.

196
00:11:06,228 --> 00:11:09,815
His stomach must be rumbling,
so he needs to eat at least this much.

197
00:11:13,652 --> 00:11:17,323
<i>Giving his all</i>
<i>and doing his best in everything</i>.

198
00:11:17,907 --> 00:11:22,745
<i>Everyone looks up to Konta,</i>
<i>who is always bright and laughing.</i>

199
00:11:22,828 --> 00:11:28,000
If I were born a bit earlier,
maybe I would flirt with you!

200
00:11:28,083 --> 00:11:29,627
Oh, you make me blush.

201
00:11:30,961 --> 00:11:32,671
Konta is…

202
00:11:32,755 --> 00:11:34,215
Konta is…

203
00:11:35,758 --> 00:11:36,926
He is an idiot.

204
00:11:37,510 --> 00:11:39,345
I think everyone knows that.

205
00:11:40,012 --> 00:11:45,142
But, I like that idiotic part of him.

206
00:11:45,851 --> 00:11:48,103
He's a fool who doesn't hurt anyone.

207
00:11:48,187 --> 00:11:51,732
Even his stupid alcohol, the flavor
isn't right unless Konta makes it.

208
00:11:51,815 --> 00:11:55,194
That drink has got to be
made by a fool, or it isn't fun.

209
00:11:55,277 --> 00:11:59,448
Since coming to this villa
and spending time with Konta,

210
00:11:59,532 --> 00:12:01,992
I've witnessed how much of an idiot he is,

211
00:12:02,660 --> 00:12:07,248
but I also see
how hard he works for his dream,

212
00:12:07,331 --> 00:12:09,166
and felt it…

213
00:12:09,959 --> 00:12:11,877
How should I put it…

214
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:15,589
It's nice. Like…

215
00:12:15,673 --> 00:12:17,800
He's charming.

216
00:12:18,926 --> 00:12:20,511
Oh, my.

217
00:12:20,594 --> 00:12:22,555
This is embarrassing!

218
00:12:23,973 --> 00:12:27,893
After coming to this villa,
I have spent so much time with him.

219
00:12:27,977 --> 00:12:29,603
It's like we're kids again.

220
00:12:30,646 --> 00:12:36,277
Well, my brother is an idiot
and usually loud and annoying.

221
00:12:36,986 --> 00:12:38,153
But…

222
00:12:38,779 --> 00:12:42,700
He is aiming to be an actor
and working so hard,

223
00:12:43,367 --> 00:12:48,080
so as his sister,
I feel I have to support him.

224
00:12:49,331 --> 00:12:52,960
Even if he's a fool,
if he can be a fool for acting,

225
00:12:53,043 --> 00:12:55,212
I guess that would be great.

226
00:12:56,338 --> 00:12:58,966
"I'll buy it because Konta Hoshino
is on the cover."

227
00:12:59,049 --> 00:13:01,510
"I'll watch it
because Konta Hoshino is in it."

228
00:13:01,594 --> 00:13:05,889
I want to create
a Konta Hoshino sensation like that.

229
00:13:07,766 --> 00:13:12,062
<i>The jobless friends who support Konta.</i>

230
00:13:13,856 --> 00:13:17,735
<i>The cool Mr. Nishigami</i>
<i>who watches over him.</i>

231
00:13:19,862 --> 00:13:22,698
<i>Konta's groundless confidence</i>…

232
00:13:22,781 --> 00:13:28,245
<i>Is his driving force to keep chasing</i>
<i>his big dream of being an actor.</i>

233
00:13:29,330 --> 00:13:32,416
<i>Someday, that confidence</i>
<i>might become real,</i>

234
00:13:32,499 --> 00:13:36,962
<i>and the day may come when the Konta</i>
<i>Hoshino boom takes the world by storm.</i>

235
00:13:40,716 --> 00:13:41,800
<i>Until that day</i>…

236
00:13:42,635 --> 00:13:45,137
<i>we want to keep watching over him.</i>

237
00:13:46,597 --> 00:13:47,765
<i>Konta!</i>

238
00:13:48,349 --> 00:13:50,726
<i>Everyone is rooting for you!</i>

239
00:13:59,026 --> 00:14:00,069
So in the end…

240
00:14:00,152 --> 00:14:03,322
It shows that Konta
is a lovable guy, right?

241
00:14:03,405 --> 00:14:04,281
Yeah.

242
00:14:04,365 --> 00:14:07,785
And my brother
didn't even watch it until the end.

243
00:14:07,868 --> 00:14:09,578
He really is an idiot.

244
00:14:10,204 --> 00:14:11,163
Oh, look.

245
00:14:11,246 --> 00:14:13,832
-What?
-The hashtag #WeedEatingMan is trending!

246
00:14:13,916 --> 00:14:16,251
-What?
-The part where he was eating mugwort?

247
00:14:16,335 --> 00:14:17,461
-Seriously?
-Look!

248
00:14:17,544 --> 00:14:19,171
-Amazing!
-It's true!

249
00:14:19,254 --> 00:14:20,881
Wow!

250
00:14:20,965 --> 00:14:21,840
Right?

251
00:14:21,924 --> 00:14:23,384
Everyone's posting.

252
00:14:23,467 --> 00:14:24,635
-Amazing.
-How stupid.

253
00:14:25,219 --> 00:14:26,345
-Amazing!
-This part…

254
00:14:26,428 --> 00:14:27,513
Oh, wow.

255
00:14:27,596 --> 00:14:28,931
-It's going viral.
-Wow.

256
00:14:29,014 --> 00:14:31,225
-How stupid.
-What a funny pic.

257
00:14:31,308 --> 00:14:33,102
-It's going viral.
-Wow!

258
00:15:02,715 --> 00:15:03,799
Konta.

259
00:15:03,882 --> 00:15:06,218
Dinner is ready. Aren't you going to eat?

260
00:15:24,278 --> 00:15:25,195
Mr. Konta.

261
00:15:25,863 --> 00:15:27,197
It's Torihara.

262
00:15:29,950 --> 00:15:32,369
I was worried, so I rushed here by car.

263
00:15:32,453 --> 00:15:35,831
I thought you might be shocked
after watching the broadcast.

264
00:15:38,834 --> 00:15:40,085
Mr. Konta,

265
00:15:40,169 --> 00:15:44,214
I think this episode
turned out quite well.

266
00:15:45,591 --> 00:15:46,759
What?

267
00:15:47,718 --> 00:15:50,471
I believe your charm
and essence as a person

268
00:15:50,554 --> 00:15:52,681
were properly conveyed to the viewers.

269
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:57,811
Are you talking about that footage?

270
00:16:01,356 --> 00:16:05,152
I was shown like an idiot,
made a laughingstock online.

271
00:16:06,070 --> 00:16:08,739
It isn't even about me
being an actor anymore!

272
00:16:10,115 --> 00:16:11,825
Everyone looks down on me.

273
00:16:13,327 --> 00:16:14,578
I'm finished.

274
00:16:16,455 --> 00:16:18,290
My acting career is over.

275
00:16:20,042 --> 00:16:21,126
Mr. Konta,

276
00:16:21,210 --> 00:16:24,963
I thought that was exactly
what makes you charming.

277
00:16:25,714 --> 00:16:26,924
What?

278
00:16:27,007 --> 00:16:28,884
Everyone wants to see flawed people.

279
00:16:28,967 --> 00:16:30,928
People grow attached to flawed people.

280
00:16:31,011 --> 00:16:33,514
That's your unique charm
that no other actor has!

281
00:16:33,597 --> 00:16:36,391
This episode conveyed that to the viewers.

282
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:40,395
Mr. Konta, you get easily carried away,

283
00:16:40,479 --> 00:16:44,274
so if I had encouraged you more,
you would have shown us more antics.

284
00:16:44,358 --> 00:16:46,193
But I thought that would be wrong.

285
00:16:46,276 --> 00:16:49,530
Actually, the producer
told me to stir you up more.

286
00:16:52,199 --> 00:16:58,497
I believe your charm, Mr. Konta,
lies in how you do your best for others

287
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:01,166
when no one is watching
and no one asked you to,

288
00:17:01,250 --> 00:17:04,336
and how purely you enjoy happiness.

289
00:17:04,419 --> 00:17:06,046
That's what I intended to film.

290
00:17:08,006 --> 00:17:11,426
Mr. Konta, you're the best
just the way you are.

291
00:17:12,136 --> 00:17:13,595
I came here to say that.

292
00:17:14,138 --> 00:17:15,514
Now, excuse me.

293
00:17:32,114 --> 00:17:33,282
Hello?

294
00:17:41,707 --> 00:17:43,709
What? What's wrong?

295
00:17:43,792 --> 00:17:45,002
It's decided!

296
00:17:45,085 --> 00:17:46,336
What is?

297
00:17:47,171 --> 00:17:48,922
-A movie!
-What?

298
00:17:49,006 --> 00:17:52,634
Apparently, a movie director who watched
the documentary is making a film

299
00:17:52,718 --> 00:17:54,344
on the Tenpo famine for his next work,

300
00:17:54,428 --> 00:17:56,847
and they want to film
a peasant eating grass,

301
00:17:56,930 --> 00:17:58,515
and he wants to cast me for it!

302
00:17:58,599 --> 00:17:59,516
Hey!

303
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,518
-You did it, Konta!
-I did it!

304
00:18:01,602 --> 00:18:03,103
The Great Tenpo famine…

305
00:18:03,187 --> 00:18:04,313
A historical piece?

306
00:18:04,396 --> 00:18:07,900
-A period movie!
-Just getting a role is wonderful!

307
00:18:07,983 --> 00:18:08,901
I'm happy!

308
00:18:08,984 --> 00:18:11,278
-You're an actor!
-Congratulations!

309
00:18:11,361 --> 00:18:12,404
Congratulations!

310
00:18:12,487 --> 00:18:13,447
Yay!

311
00:18:13,530 --> 00:18:15,824
Konta! Congratulations!

312
00:18:17,159 --> 00:18:18,410
Congratulations!

313
00:18:18,493 --> 00:18:19,536
Wow!

314
00:18:19,620 --> 00:18:21,830
-You did it!
-Thanks, Rinrin.

315
00:18:21,914 --> 00:18:24,750
Congratulations! You really did it!

316
00:18:47,105 --> 00:18:48,232
Who might you be?

317
00:18:48,315 --> 00:18:49,816
Focus!

318
00:18:51,401 --> 00:18:52,736
<i>Obon </i>holidays, huh.

319
00:18:52,819 --> 00:18:54,655
What do we do on <i>Obon</i>, again?

320
00:18:54,738 --> 00:18:58,951
<i>Shouldn't we at least visit Midori's</i>
<i>grandma's grave? She built this villa.</i>

321
00:18:59,034 --> 00:19:01,578
-Grandma's photos!
-Wow!

322
00:19:02,579 --> 00:19:03,872
Ta-da!

323
00:19:03,956 --> 00:19:05,666
Oh, so cute!

324
00:19:05,749 --> 00:19:08,168
-Yay!
-So cute.

325
00:19:08,252 --> 00:19:10,837
Hey, the two of them left together!

326
00:19:11,672 --> 00:19:14,967
<i>This way</i>
<i>Grandma can return to the villa too.</i>

327
00:19:15,842 --> 00:19:18,553
<i>I'm home, Mr. Nishigami.</i>

328
00:19:19,054 --> 00:19:21,098
<i>Did you get a girlfriend?</i>

329
00:19:22,182 --> 00:19:26,895
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

